{
  "name": "vector_light_two_lights",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "Two emitters, one long occluder, and the question only a PER-EMITTER composition can answer: what happens to a cell that one lamp cannot see and the other can. Two lamps sit close to a seven-cell wall, offset well above and below it, so the wall throws two shadows that overlap in three separable zones \u2014 directly behind it neither lamp can see, and at each end exactly one can. A composition that zeroes a cell's artificial light wholesale cannot tell those apart. Phase 3 subtracts each emitter's own contribution separately, so the single-shadowed zones should keep the light of whichever lamp still sees them while the doubly-shadowed zone keeps neither. Five arms: vanilla, the shipped crossfade, phase 3's mask alone, the mask WITH the additive beam on top of it, and full 27. Every arm states every flag rather than inheriting one.",
